Z||000000||Ronnie||08-09-2001||10:34 PM||||My rear hatch release decided it would stop working yesterday(electric).It, and the door locks are on the same fuse, but the locks are still working. Can anyone tell me what to check next?I changed out the dash switch with another one , didn't help.||||reg||9
Z||000001||GT-maniac||08-09-2001||10:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ronnie:<BR><B>My rear hatch release decided it would stop working yesterday(electric).It, and the door locks are on the same fuse, but the locks are still working. Can anyone tell me what to check next?I changed out the dash switch with another one , didn't help.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Did you verify with a tester that there is power at the lock soleniod ? I'd check that next.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||08-10-2001||11:29 AM||||When you push the button do you hear the relay click?  If not you probably need to replace the relay.  I believe it is in the dash near the release button (not sure though).||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||08-10-2001||11:39 AM||||It's under the dash, on the left side of the steering column.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||08-10-2001||08:43 PM||||Someone refresh my memory . . . Does the emergency brake have to be on for this circuit to work?  Could be a problem with that.  Relay is a good chance, too.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||08-10-2001||09:09 PM||||If it's a manual trans and the ignition switch is on the e-brake has to be engaged. The relay acts as an interlock rather than a power relay. Supposedly you shouldn't be able to pop the trunk while driveing down the road.||||reg||1
Z||000006||x-thumpr-x||08-10-2001||10:43 PM||||your e-brake has nothing to do with your release. I have an 84 manual, and have the little brake sensor disconnected from mine. The pinging gets annouying while your parked and running! Mine works no problem. my car though has to have the ignition in the run position for the relase to work though||||reg||1
Z||000007||DRH||08-10-2001||11:21 PM||||My 88 manual has to have the parking brake on if the key is on. With the key off it will work with the brake off but the brake light will flash. <P>The relay is next to the steering column (I thought right side but could be left). It will have a Gray/Black (from switch), Black/White (to trunk ) and either a tan/white (manual) or a yellow (automatic).<P>If you unplug the relay and jumper gray/black to black/white the switch should pop the trunk any time.<P>I've heard 84 is different but don't know personally.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ronnie||08-10-2001||11:33 PM||||Thanks guys , will check out that relay , it's not clicking.||||reg||12
Z||000009||Primaris||08-10-2001||11:38 PM||||Wait!  Look to see if the little ground wire is still connected to the back of the deck lid.  It is located on the passenger side near the rear window.  On my '86 the trunk will not release unless this clip is attached.<BR>Oops, Drivers side.<BR>------------------<BR>Signatures are a waste of bandwidth!<p>[This message has been edited by Primaris (edited 08-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Mickey_Moose||08-11-2001||01:37 PM||||Yes, check the ground wire, drivers side (from hinge to deck lid)<P>...also the plug on the passenger side, attached to the hinge, make sure it is also connected together.<P>The relay does not 'click' if either of these are disconnected. (at least on my car)<P>Tim||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||08-11-2001||03:17 PM||||you can also sub the horn relay for the trunk relay as a test. horn relay is electrically the same but a heavier duty part. If it's the relay just get another horn relay to replace it.||||reg||1
